codex
The Python implementation now uses recursive insertion sort and an explicit recursive popcount, so it depends on no Python sorting or binary-formatting built-ins. That keeps both the translator surface and the K semantics small enough to audit: functions, conditionals, calls, integer operations, lists, indexing, and tail slices. Negative inputs terminate using magnitude-based popcount, while the universal correctness claim will remain scoped to the prompt’s stated non-negative domain.
